<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CHILL_HEATED_SUIT_1 — the heated dive suit, one clock (a battery charge
  gauge; card ruling declined both the two-clock heat+air option and the
  no-clock option). Full mechanism, Odyssey-research writeup and the
  hypothermia-math this leans on: RM_CompHeatedSuitBattery.cs's own header.

  ParentName="Apparel_Vacsuit" DELIBERATELY — Odyssey already ships exactly
  "the appropriate suit type" (Defs/Odyssey/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.
  xml, MEASURED via RimSage this session): real shipped art, armor,
  insulation, EquipDelay, body coverage, even the "restricts movement"
  framing, all for free. This def inherits that whole shape and only
  overrides what the Chill's own ruling actually asks for: Insulation_Cold
  cut from the inherited 90 down to a modest 20 (see the .cs header — the
  full -110C counteraction is charge-gated via RM_StatPart_HeatedSuitCharge,
  not a static apparel stat, or an empty suit would still be halfway safe)
  and the battery comp itself.

  ART: reuses Odyssey's real Vacsuit texture/wornGraphicPath outright
  (Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit) with a warm tint —
  legitimate shipped DLC art for exactly this kind of garment, not a
  placeholder standing in for a mismatched subject. infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending}/registry.jsonl carries nothing for "suit"/"heated"/"vacuum"
  this session (checked before writing this file) — nothing to reuse from
  our own pipeline, and nothing further queued: this art already fits.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="Apparel_Vacsuit" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RM_ChillHeatedSuit</defName>
    <label>heated dive suit</label>
    <description>A vacuum-rated suit rebuilt around a battery-fed heating web instead of a passive shell — it recycles the wearer's air same as any vacsuit, but the real work is the coils. On the Chill's seabed the ambient cold alone would kill in hours; this is the only thing standing between a working pawn and that. The gauge on its own wrist display is not a fuel light. When it reads empty, the suit is just a heavy coat, and the cold does not wait.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/Vacsuit/Vacsuit</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.9</drawSize>
      <color>(214, 108, 48)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <!-- Everything else (MaxHitPoints, Mass, ArmorRating_*, Insulation_
           Heat, EquipDelay, WorkToMake) is inherited unchanged from
           Apparel_Vacsuit — RimWorld's def-inheritance merges statBases by
           tag, so only the one stat actually being changed needs stating.
           Insulation_Cold: cut from the inherited 90. See file header and
           the .cs header for why the static value must be modest — the
           real -110C protection is 100% charge-gated. -->
      <Insulation_Cold>20</Insulation_Cold>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.DivingInteraction.RM_CompProperties_HeatedSuitBattery">
        <maxChargeTicks>15000</maxChargeTicks>
        <drainIntervalTicks>250</drainIntervalTicks>
        <rechargeRateMultiplier>3</rechargeRateMultiplier>
        <chargerSearchRadius>3.9</chargerSearchRadius>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
